sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / Data Scientist
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant MutWH as Mutating Webhook<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Controller as RayCluster Controller
    participant RouteAPI as OpenShift Route API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant ExtUser as External User
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant OAuth as OAuth Proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Dashboard as Ray Dashboard<br/>8265/TCP HTTP
    participant OSAuth as OpenShift OAuth<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    rect rgb(232, 244, 253)
        Note over User,Dashboard: Flow 1: RayCluster Creation on OpenShift
        User->>K8sAPI: 1. Create RayCluster CR<br/>HTTPS/443, Bearer Token
        K8sAPI->>MutWH: 2. Admission webhook call<br/>HTTPS/9443, TLS (cert-controller)
        MutWH->>MutWH: 3. Inject oauth-proxy sidecar,<br/>TLS volumes, mTLS init containers
        MutWH-->>K8sAPI: Mutated RayCluster spec
        K8sAPI-->>Controller: 4. Watch event: RayCluster created
        Controller->>K8sAPI: 4a. Create OAuth Service, SA,<br/>CRB, NetworkPolicies, Secrets<br/>HTTPS/443, SA token
        Controller->>RouteAPI: 5. Create Dashboard Route (reencrypt)<br/>+ Client Route (passthrough)<br/>HTTPS/443, SA token
        RouteAPI-->>Controller: Routes created
    end

    rect rgb(255, 242, 204)
        Note over ExtUser,Dashboard: Flow 1 (continued): User Accesses Ray Dashboard
        ExtUser->>Route: 6. Access Ray Dashboard<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS (reencrypt)
        Route->>OAuth: Forward to oauth-proxy<br/>HTTPS/8443
        OAuth->>OSAuth: Authenticate user<br/>HTTPS/443, OAuth
        OSAuth-->>OAuth: Auth response
        OAuth->>Dashboard: 7. Proxy to Ray Dashboard<br/>HTTP/8265 (localhost)
        Dashboard-->>OAuth: Dashboard response
        OAuth-->>Route: Authenticated response
        Route-->>ExtUser: Dashboard UI
    end

    rect rgb(240, 248, 232)
        Note over Controller,Dashboard: Flow 2: mTLS Certificate Provisioning
        Controller->>K8sAPI: 1. Create CA Secret<br/>(RSA 2048, self-signed, 1yr)<br/>HTTPS/443, SA token
        Note over Controller: Init container mounts<br/>CA Secret as volume
        Note over Controller: Init container generates<br/>server cert to emptyDir
        Note over Dashboard: Ray head ↔ workers<br/>gRPC/10001, mTLS<br/>(operator-generated certs)
    end
